<title>BELGIUM: Germany holds 88 pct of EU intervention grain.</title>
<headline>Germany holds 88 pct of EU intervention grain.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany holds 88 percent of the 2.1 million tonnes of grain held or being offered into European Union intervention stores, European Commission figures showed.</p>
<p>			EU Intervention Grain Stocks 1996/97 (tonnes):</p>
<p>			Net Stocks    Grain on   Total	Start of</p>
<p>					  Offer		     Season</p>
<p>			 5/6/97	 5/6/97     5/6/97     1/6/96</p>
<p>			1,717,104     333,095    2,050,199  2,596,112</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p> Germany	    1,549,925     244,685    1,794,610  2,432,365</p>
<p> Ireland		 66,745	19,572	 86,317     62,011</p>
<p> Finland		 24,606	35,652	 60,258     47,899</p>
<p> Denmark		 50,537	 4,500	 55,037     67,751</p>
<p> Italy		   12,903	   -	   12,903     15,264</p>
<p> Britain		 11,078	   298	 11,376	  -</p>
<p> Greece		   1,310	   -	    1,310	1,310</p>
<p> France		     -	  16,230	 16,230     12,328</p>
<p> Austria		    -	  12,158	 12,158	  -</p>
<p> Other countries	  -	     -		-	    -</p>
